  23:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****   ==============================================================================
  24:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****                       ##### RCC specific features #####
  25:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****   ==============================================================================
  26:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****     [..]
  27:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       After reset the device is running from Internal High Speed oscillator
  28:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (HSI 16MHz) with Flash 0 wait state, Flash prefetch buffer, D-Cache
  29:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       and I-Cache are disabled, and all peripherals are off except internal
  30:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       SRAM, Flash and JTAG.
  31:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) There is no prescaler on High speed (AHB) and Low speed (APB) busses;
  32:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****           all peripherals mapped on these busses are running at HSI speed.
ARM GAS  /var/folders/8x/_y6g3dfs0698dfd49y4vcg_w0000gn/T//ccCx5Rca.s 			page 2


  33:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) The clock for all peripherals is switched off, except the SRAM and FLASH.
  34:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) All GPIOs are in input floating state, except the JTAG pins which
  35:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****           are assigned to be used for debug purpose.
  36:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
  37:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****     [..]
  38:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       Once the device started from reset, the user application has to:
  39:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) Configure the clock source to be used to drive the System clock
  40:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****           (if the application needs higher frequency/performance)
  41:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) Configure the System clock frequency and Flash settings
  42:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) Configure the AHB and APB busses prescalers
  43:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) Enable the clock for the peripheral(s) to be used
  44:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) Configure the clock source(s) for peripherals which clocks are not
  45:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****           derived from the System clock (I2S, RTC, ADC, USB OTG FS/SDIO/RNG)
  46:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
  47:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****                       ##### RCC Limitations #####
  48:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****   ==============================================================================
  49:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****     [..]
  50:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       A delay between an RCC peripheral clock enable and the effective peripheral
  51:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       enabling should be taken into account in order to manage the peripheral read/write
  52:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       from/to registers.
  53:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) This delay depends on the peripheral mapping.
  54:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) If peripheral is mapped on AHB: the delay is 2 AHB clock cycle
  55:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****           after the clock enable bit is set on the hardware register
  56:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) If peripheral is mapped on APB: the delay is 2 APB clock cycle
  57:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****           after the clock enable bit is set on the hardware register
  58:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
  59:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****     [..]
  60:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       Implemented Workaround:
  61:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****       (+) For AHB & APB peripherals, a dummy read to the peripheral register has been
  62:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****           inserted in each __HAL_RCC_PPP_CLK_ENABLE() macro.
  63:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c **** 
  64:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****   @endverbatim
  65:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_rcc.c ****   ******************************************************************************
